{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106981","id":2556026273,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6YWd2h","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106981","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106981.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106981.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106981","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106981/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106981/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106981/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/215022d863005683daf86f82961e2318ab8771f5","number":106981,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix Texture2DArray import error by updating webp saving functions","user":{"login":"Haha64142","id":173843531,"node_id":"U_kgDOClykSw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173843531?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Haha64142","html_url":"https://github.com/Haha64142","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Haha64142/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Haha64142/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Haha64142/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Haha64142/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Haha64142/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Haha64142/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Haha64142/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Haha64142/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Haha64142/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"When importing a Texture2DArray with lossless or lossy compression, Godot would throw an error saying that multiple image formats were used in the array. This was due to the way the webp module saved and loaded images. (See issue #106627)\r\n\r\nIn the webp module, Godot would normally save and load the image by checking the image if it contained an alhpa pixels. This would cause issues when saving a Texture2DArray because each layer would be saved with its own format, which could reseult in different format versions being used for each layer.\r\n\r\nIn the _webp_packer function, the code would check if the image had alpha pixels and then pack the image using that format. This would lead to the previously mentioned issue. I changed the function to use the format that was provided to the function if possible. If the format is not supported, it will fall back to the original behavior of checking for alpha pixels.\r\n\r\nIn the _webp_unpack function, I updated the code to unpack the image using the format that the image was saved with. This ensures that the layers in Texture2DArray would all have the same format, preventing the import error.\r\n\r\nFixes #106627","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":890310502,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4OTAzMTA1MDI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:import","name":"topic:import","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2025-05-31T01:53:47Z","updated_at":"2025-07-29T08:05:14Z","closed_at":"2025-07-29T00:57:05Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit